## Rules for Agents

- Do **not** create or update files under `tasks/` — that folder was removed.
- Put the full acceptance criteria and spec in the issue body. Do not add a Story Status or task Status column — use the project **Status** field.
- Link child tasks to their parent story issue in the **Story** project field and in the task body.
- When starting a story, move the **Story** issue **Status** → **In Progress** on the project board.
- When starting a task, move that **Task** issue **Status** → **In Progress** on the project board.
- When committing completed task work, **wait for explicit user approval** after implementation is ready for review. Then use subject line `<task_number>: <short description>`, move the task's project **Status** to **Done**, and add `Closes #N` in the commit body when ready to close the issue on push. **Never commit without user review.**
- Never add `Co-authored-by` (or any other trailer) to commit messages unless the user explicitly asks for it.
- After completing a story, update [`docs/DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md`](../../docs/DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md) if the roadmap changed.
